<title>USA: US to sell $30.75 bln of 2-, 5-yr notes Oct 22, 23.</title>
<headline>US to sell $30.75 bln of 2-, 5-yr notes Oct 22, 23.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Treasury Department said on Wednesday it would sell $18.25 billion of two-year notes on October 22, and $12.5 bln of five-year notes on October 23, to refund $26.936 billion of securities maturing October 31 and to raise $3.825 billion of new cash.</p>
<p>The notes will be issued October 31. The two-year notes mature Oct 31, 1998, and the five-year notes mature Oct 31, 2001.</p>
<p>The CUSIP number for the 2-year notes will be 912827Z70, and for the five-year notes will be 912827Z88.</p>
